  },
  "question": {
    "text": "<p>A planar frame is made of thin uniform rods. The length of section AB and EF is <math><msub><mi>l</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;and its coefficient of linear expansion is <math><msub><mi>&#945;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>. The length of section CD is <math><msub><mi>l</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;and its coefficient of linear expansion is <math><msub><mi>&#945;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>. CB and DE are of the same length having coefficient of linear expansion <math><msub><mi>&#945;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>. Points A, B, E and F reside on same line, that is, sections AB and EF overlap. Then the ratio <math><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>l</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>l</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></math>&nbsp;for which the distance between end A and end F remains the same at all temperatures is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msub><mi>&#945;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mrow><mi>n</mi><msub><mi>&#945;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></math> then find the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi></math>.</p>\r\r<p><br />\r<img src=\"assets\\qt0012_99c598729629.jpeg\" /></p>\r"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "2",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>For distance between A and F to remain constant, extension in CD = extension in AB + extension in EF<br /><br /><math><mo>&#8756;</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#916;</mi><msub><mrow><mi>l</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#916;</mi><msub><mrow><mi>l</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><msub><mrow><mi>l</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mi>&#945;</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#916;</mi><msub><mrow><mi>&#952;</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mrow><mi>l</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mi>&#945;</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#916;</mi><mi>&#952;</mi></math><br /><br />Or <math><mfrac><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>l</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>l</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>&#945;</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><msub><mrow><mi>&#945;</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math></p>"
  }
}